easure let me give you an example  i don't want to go on a too great length  the cost  of  making a building more efficient  has gone up by over three times thanks  to this measure  the prices  or the price of investing  in  refurbishments  has  almost tripled because this 110  measure  means that there's no incentive for  people to bargain on prices so that's  the result but in any case things are  moving forward in parliament the  government has done what it can do and  our minister for the environment is  excellent  now  changes to the recovery and resilience  plan  well the first  problem  here  is to ensure  that  public  works  continues and that new tenders open up  and yesterday the government earmarked 3  billion essentially to enable businesses  to recover 90  of the increase in raw materials costs  this measure was welcomed  by industry of course  industry that is involved in business  building infrastructure and is involved  in public works but actually was  welcomed right across the board and this  is the path that we've chosen  so before we talk about  changing the recovery and resilience  plan let's make it work i mean it's not  old hat at all  we've respected all our objectives will  continue to do it by the end of june and  we'll do the same at the end of december  so it's certainly not  outdated i mean if it does become  necessary to change certain things in  some points for some sectors yes but  specific investments we don't want to  change the recovery and resilience plan  completely i mean there are certain  minor changes that might have to be made  and if there are then we will make those  changes  so those were the things  that i wanted to say in terms of  specific matters  but now  let me  move on  to the overall  vision that  we're talking about today and i think  the nature  of what we're talking about is that we  basically share  ideals projects and ideas the european  union  faces many challenges  i  would like to agree with the last  political group speaker who said that  the most important challenge we face is  peace  and that's clearly the main goal that we  need to move towards  the european  union  is  acting along those lines as is my  government but there are many other  things that we want to achieve as well  and  when it comes to all these challenges  the response is that more integration is  the best way to go is the best way to  deal with all these challenges i talked  about pragmatic federalism  and that means that for many of these  challenges the only way to go  is to tackle them together and that  doesn't only mean pooling our funding i  mean i'm a banker and people think that  the only thing i think about is money  but  that's not  the only thing we can do  dealing with challenges together means  designing the solutions together it  means monitoring what we're doing  together it means ensuring that all of  us ensure that the money is spent  properly and italy is fully aware of  that and as you all know because i've  said it many times italy  is aware that it has a great  responsibility when it comes to spending  these funds that have come under the  next generation fund appropriately  and we will also be responsible when it  comes  to decisions on energy and decisions on  public investment also the digital and  green transitions  these are challenges  which  are  major in scope you know that uh certain  calculations have been made on the  digital and green transitions and  according to those calculations  by 2030 the funding need for the entire  european union is around two trillion  euros and these aren't figures  that national budgets can come up with  on defense  well again there are two goals  firstly strategic independence  and we've said several times that a  strong europe means a strong nato but in  order to achieve strategic autonomy as i  said in my introduction the first step  is to ensure that our military  expenditure is more efficient  as i said earlier we spend three times  as much as russia and it would be  unthinkable to do anything effective  without making our defense expenditure  more effective and more coordinated and  that's why i've called for a conference  to look towards that goal  i share  the need of  achieving  independence when it comes to  producing certain things that are  essential for our continent microchips  for example  that's  one example but there are other things  that are crucial for our supply chains  and  we need strategic independence  for those things  the war but also  before the war recent events i think  have shown that  production chains and markets don't  always  work in a fluid manner  and problems and bottlenecks can lead to  serious crises so we need to tackle  those challenges as well  that's this pragmatic federalism but i  also talked about perfect  federalism  the federalism of ideals and our values  are currently facing challenges that are  unprecedented since the launching of the  european union and given those  challenges we need to stand together  that's  where  this federalism of ideals can be seen we  need to find solutions that are joint  solutions  in spite of the fact that we're all very  different because of our histories our  traditions because of our starting  points and that's  the real difficulty that we have to get  over  and we need to deal with that difficulty  in order to be successful as europe  and let me conclude  now  by saying  that  if all of this  requires  a procedure of treaty change  let's go for treaty change  bravely and in a confident manner  thank you very much prime minister  draghi and that closes this debate and  we move on to the next one thank you  very very much to all  you

